<h2>Asobi 1.0 (build 1734) <span class="when">Oct 21, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Showcase viewing</b> shows how each viewer&#8217;s connection did: its speed against what the piece needs, how long the picture took to come up and the piece to start, and any stops to load. Per visit, summed up above the visits, and in the CSV.</li>
<li><b>Conform reports</b> list a shot&#8217;s plates as its source when its clips came from outside the cut (a color ref, an email), and no longer count the cut&#8217;s stand-in for it as missing. A new section, Plates from outside the cut, lists them with where their ranges came from.</li>
<li><b>Finding media</b> no longer takes a file whose name merely starts with the same eight letters for the one the cut names.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1728) <span class="when">Oct 20, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Recording a session</b> no longer turns the call and the clip audio down on your Mac while it records.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1724) <span class="when">Oct 19, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Update from Kitsu Playlist.</b> Media menu, or the circling arrows at the top of the Playlist: late shots and new versions from the same Kitsu playlist come into a running review, and go out to everyone in it, on the web and in Asobi.</li>
<li><b>Export Compare with Edit Ref.</b> Media &#9656; Conformed Cut: the conform beside its Edit Ref as one QuickTime, lined up as Compare Edit Ref shows it.</li>
<li><b>Conform reports</b> show a picture for every stacked layer (PL02, PL03).</li>
<li><b>Plate review movies</b> are always 16:9, a plate of another shape kept whole inside it, so Kitsu shows it unstretched.</li>
<li><b>A pull of many plates</b> makes each review movie and proxy from its own plate, never another one in the same folder.</li>
<li><b>Studio-made shots</b> get their own card, and a shot in the cut with no footage gets its placeholder, pulled or not.</li>
<li><b>A re-cut</b> keeps a shot&#8217;s name when its file isn&#8217;t on this Mac.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1711) <span class="when">Oct 19, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>A reel&#8217;s slates stay clean.</b> Burn-ins are drawn on the shots only, never over a slate or a gap.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1708) <span class="when">Oct 19, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Slates carry the studio and the review.</b> The Autonomy wordmark sits at the foot (another studio&#8217;s Report Setup logo, beside its name), and under the title the review in figures: project, client, date, how many shots and the running time. A title that nearly fits stays on one line.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1705) <span class="when">Oct 19, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Slates, redrawn.</b> Insert Slate makes a card in Asobi&#8217;s own type: the title large, the project and date beneath it, your notes as a reading paragraph, and the studio along the foot. It&#8217;s drawn at the review&#8217;s own size, and typing -- gives a dash.</li>
<li><b>Review notes go to Kitsu as they&#8217;re made.</b> While you host a review of a Kitsu playlist, each frame with notes or marks becomes a comment on its shot&#8217;s task, with the marked frame as a picture, half a minute after the last change there. Edits and deletes follow into Kitsu, and End Review sends anything still waiting. Turn it off in the Kitsu window.</li>
<li><b>Reels for a client.</b> Playback &#9656; Source &#9656; Flip All to Source Media puts every clip on its full-resolution render. Burn in &#9656; Subtle draws small, quiet type with no plates: the shot and version, the timecode, the studio and date. The Whole Session Reel can now be Source size, UHD, HD or 1280&#160;&#215;&#160;720.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1698) <span class="when">Oct 19, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Joining a review brings in every clip.</b> A Mac that joins while the host is in the review gets the whole playlist, in the host&#8217;s order, not just the clip the host is on. Clips this Mac doesn&#8217;t have play as the review&#8217;s copies.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1695) <span class="when">Oct 19, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li>Improvements and fixes.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
